# The five tables

The downsets of $`t_1, \ldots, t_5` are

$$`{\downarrow}t_1 = \{t_0, t_1\} \qquad {\downarrow}t_2 = \{t_0, t_2\} \qquad {\downarrow}t_3 = \{t_0, t_1, t_2, t_3\} \qquad {\downarrow}t_4 = \{t_0, t_1, t_4\} \qquad {\downarrow}t_5 = \{t_0, t_1, \ldots, t_5\}`

up to $`\dashv\vdash`, with $`t_0 = \bot`.  Each is a table in the sense above.
PROVED.

