The closure conditions of the five tables are 224 interderivabilities and 17
derivabilities between named formulas.  Each derivability is a closed
tableau of the subframe tableau calculus of the library, found by its
untrusted producer, checked by the kernel (`decide +kernel` on the checker)
and translated into a natural-deduction derivation by the calculus's
translation theorem; an interderivability is two of them.  Nothing in a cell
is trusted but the kernel check.  The cells that carry the modal content are
those for $`j_a`; three of them, the ones a proof by hand needs, are

