# The modality-free instance

The $`\bigcirc`-free instance of these covers is the Rieger–Nishimura ladder
itself, which was settled first: among its first nine rungs the covers are
computed from the truth sets on the ladder and checked by `decide`.  Restricted to
$`r_0, \ldots, r_5` they are the same seven covers.  PROVED.

{stmt}`covers9_eq`

{docstring covers9_eq +allowMissing}

{srcLink}`covers9_eq`

What the tables add is that no variable-free formula containing $`\bigcirc`
falls into these seven intervals either.  The tables stop at $`t_5`, so the
ladder's cover $`r_3 \lessdot r_6` has no counterpart here.

# Axioms

As recorded in the file (`#axioms_within`): every declaration of this section
is within `propext`, `Quot.sound`.  `#print axioms` on the build reports no
axioms for `red_box`, `red_imp` and `red_or`; `propext` alone for
`DownTable.classify`, `DownTable.classify_below`, the five tables, the three
modal cells and `low_trichotomy`; and `propext`, `Quot.sound` for the seven
covers.  `covers9_eq` (`wip/ladder8.lean`) is pinned at no axioms.
